    "summary": "Built the \u00a717 walking skeleton as npm workspaces: apps/web (Phaser client with landing page, HUD, keyboard adapter, input sender, snapshot interpolation), apps/server (Colyseus MatchRoom: one room per private match, filterBy code, static onAuth refusing protocol mismatch/unknown code/full match, 60 Hz setFixedTimestep with world logic every third step, Schema mirror patched at 20 Hz, InputGate dropping malformed/oversized/stale/future-frame/over-rate input), packages/simulation (integer fixed-point state, seeded mulberry32 in state, spawn slots, hashState = FNV-1a 64 over canonical JSON), packages/protocol (version, zod join/input schemas, validation), packages/content (sea map, spawn slots, ship speed, slice/alpha presets, \u00a78 frame budgets with validators), packages/test-tools (HeadlessClient on @colyseus/sdk). Added README.md, docs/architecture.md, the CLAUDE.md commands line, and READMEs for assets/source, assets/exported and infra. Checks I ran: I copied the tree to a fresh directory and ran npm ci with an empty cache, then all five policy checks there. typecheck passed, test:unit passed (70 tests), test:integration passed (8 tests), build passed, and the Playwright browser run with --reporter=json --workers=1 --retries=0 CI=1 passed 2 of 2. check-report --all accepted both scenarios. In the worktree I also ran integration three more times and the browser spec twice more; all passed. Nothing is committed: the task forbids commits.",
